.SH "Enumeration Type Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "enum \fBstumpless_severity\fP"

.PP
All possible severity codes available to log entries\&. In versions prior to 2\&.0\&.0, these values were simply #define symbols\&. They have been changed to an enum to clearly convey proper usage\&.
.PP
See \fBSTUMPLESS_FOREACH_SEVERITY()\fP and \fBSTUMPLESS_GENERATE_ENUM()\fP for how the enumeration is actually defined\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v2\&.0\&.0\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBEnumerator\fP
.in +1c
.TP
\fB\fISTUMPLESS_SEVERITY_EMERG \fP\fP
Emergency: system is unusable\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISTUMPLESS_SEVERITY_ALERT \fP\fP
Alert: action must be taken immediately\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISTUMPLESS_SEVERITY_CRIT \fP\fP
Critical: critical conditions\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISTUMPLESS_SEVERITY_ERR \fP\fP
Error: error conditions\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISTUMPLESS_SEVERITY_WARNING \fP\fP
Warning: warning conditions\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISTUMPLESS_SEVERITY_NOTICE \fP\fP
Notice: normal but significant condition\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISTUMPLESS_SEVERITY_INFO \fP\fP
Informational: informational messages\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISTUMPLESS_SEVERITY_DEBUG \fP\fP
Debug: debug-level messages\&. 
