.SS "enum \fBstumpless_severity\fP stumpless_get_severity_enum (const char * severity_string)"

.PP
Gets the enum value corresponding to the given severity string\&. \fBThread Safety: MT-Safe\fP This function is thread safe\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Safe\fP This function is safe to call from signal handlers\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Safe\fP This function is safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v2\&.1\&.0\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIseverity_string\fP The severity name to get the enum from\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The enum integer corresponding to the given severity or -1 if the string is not a valid severity name\&. An error code STUMPLESS_INVALID_SEVERITY is raised if the string is not a valid severity name\&. 
.RE
